Description: QuartzFire SSL inspection (Squid ssl_bump TLS interception)
 TLS decryption/inspection for QuartzFire (VyOS-based NGFW), equivalent to
 WatchGuard Fireware's Content Inspection. Squid is the SOLE TLS terminator on
 the box: it owns ssl_bump, the inspection root CA, the private key, and the
 generated-certificate store. Traffic on the configured interfaces is
 transparently redirected to Squid, peeked for SNI, spliced (passed through)
 for do-not-inspect domains, and bumped (decrypted) otherwise.
 .
 A single Rust multi-call binary (qzssl) provides the `service quartzfire
 ssl-inspection` conf-mode owner, the CA lifecycle, the plain-HTTP CA
 distribution page (:4126), the Squid build-capability probe, and the
 status plumbing the QuartzFire WebUI reads. The ICAP adaptation seam is
 pre-wired but idle — a future content-filter engine (e2guardian in ICAP mode,
 c-icap/ClamAV) attaches behind Squid as a pure filtering consumer and must
 NEVER enable its own TLS MITM or hold its own CA (see design.md).
